{
  "title": "photodiode",
  "summary": "Screen-sync input. A BPW34 photodiode sits on the end of a twisted-pair cable (it is not on this board) plugged into J1, a 2-pin JST PH (the same connector as the battery): pin 1 to the cathode, pin 2 to the anode. R1/C1 feed the reverse bias from the analog rail through a filter, so cable pickup cannot reach +3.3V. The photocurrent flows through R2 (1k, cable isolation) into R3 (load) with C2, a ~1 ms low-pass that smooths monitor backlight PWM. PD_OUT goes to a spare ADS131M08 channel, measured against GND, so every flash is sampled at the same instant as the EEG. Keep the white-patch level under the ADC's +1.2 V full scale: lower R3 if the screen is bright.",
